  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Dell Federal Systems L P obligated $1.6B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Dell Federal Systems L P won 519 awards in the period and the average award size was $3M. Dell Federal Systems L P saw obligations up 17.1% year over year. Dell Federal Systems L P generated most obligations in software and related services: Software Publishers accounts for $1.3B and a second Software Publishers entry accounts for $126M. Dell Federal Systems L P also recorded obligations in Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $66.3M and Other Computer Related Services at $63.3M. Dell Federal Systems L P recorded Computer Storage Device Manufacturing at $4.6M and Computer and Computer Peripheral Equipment and Software Merchant Wholesalers at $743K. Dell Federal Systems L P recorded Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $617K and several smaller NAICS markets including Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $94.8K, Other Electronic Component Manufacturing at $44.3K, and Facilities Support Services at $24.9K. FY2026 to date totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Dell Federal Systems L P's largest federal buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $553M. The Department of Defense obligated $405M and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $283M. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $138M, and other agencies on the list include the Department of Commerce at $59.2M and the Department of Transportation at $52M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and product types drive Dell Federal Systems L P's obligations?",
        "body": "Software Publishers is the dominant market with $1.3B and a second Software Publishers entry at $126M. Electronic Computer Manufacturing and Other Computer Related Services follow with $66.3M and $63.3M respectively. Dell Federal Systems L P also has obligations in Computer Storage Device Manufacturing at $4.6M and several niche markets under NAICS with values ranging from $743K down to $24.9K."
      }
    ]
  },
